1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,300
You type M V N package. Maven prints a wall of lines. Which ones matter?

2
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:07,391
Package is not one step.

3
00:00:07,391 --> 00:00:08,997
It is the end of a chain,

4
00:00:08,997 --> 00:00:10,988
and Maven runs the whole chain,

5
00:00:10,988 --> 00:00:12,079
in a fixed order.

6
00:00:12,629 --> 00:00:16,747
Today you learn that order, the life cycle, and which tool runs at each step.

7
00:00:17,297 --> 00:00:22,161
You will see it live, then break it on purpose, then fix a failing project yourself.

8
00:00:22,711 --> 00:00:23,780
One honest note.

9
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:27,056
My recording computer cannot reach Maven Central,

10
00:00:27,056 --> 00:00:31,201
so these demos use a local copy of the libraries and plug ins.

11
00:00:31,201 --> 00:00:34,209
The commands are the same ones you will type.

12
00:00:35,759 --> 00:00:41,348
Maven has three built-in life cycles. Clean. Default. And site, for documentation.

13
00:00:41,898 --> 00:00:44,842
Clean has one job. Delete the target folder.

14
00:00:45,392 --> 00:00:47,483
Default builds your project.

15
00:00:47,483 --> 00:00:48,678
Its main phases,

16
00:00:48,678 --> 00:00:50,096
in order: validate,

17
00:00:50,096 --> 00:00:50,694
compile,

18
00:00:50,694 --> 00:00:51,067
test,

19
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:51,664
package,

20
00:00:51,664 --> 00:00:52,187
verify,

21
00:00:52,187 --> 00:00:52,784
install,

22
00:00:52,784 --> 00:00:53,307
deploy.

23
00:00:53,857 --> 00:00:58,124
The golden rule. Run a phase, and Maven runs every phase before it.

24
00:00:58,674 --> 00:01:00,854
So M V N package also compiles,

25
00:01:00,854 --> 00:01:02,612
and also runs your tests.

26
00:01:02,612 --> 00:01:05,074
You never ask for those separately.

27
00:01:05,624 --> 00:01:10,296
And a phase on its own does nothing. It is an empty slot, waiting for a plug in.

28
00:01:12,346 --> 00:01:18,234
Plug ins do the real work. Each plug in offers goals, and Maven binds a goal to a phase.

29
00:01:18,784 --> 00:01:21,877
Phase: compile. Goal: compiler, compile.

30
00:01:22,427 --> 00:01:28,358
Phase: test. Goal: sure fire, test. Sure fire is the plug in that runs your unit tests.

31
00:01:28,908 --> 00:01:33,367
Phase: package. Goal: jar, jar. It packs your classes into a jar.

32
00:01:33,917 --> 00:01:36,693
And two more run before compile: resources,

33
00:01:36,693 --> 00:01:37,338
resources,

34
00:01:37,338 --> 00:01:38,888
which copies your files,

35
00:01:38,888 --> 00:01:41,341
and the same again for test resources.

36
00:01:41,891 --> 00:01:46,371
Remember the shape: phase, then the goal bound to it. We are about to see it live.

37
00:01:48,421 --> 00:01:51,578
Go to the demo project. Type: CD, demo.

38
00:01:52,128 --> 00:02:02,710
Start small. Type: mvn -B compile | grep -E '^\[INFO\] --- |BUILD' | cut -c8-

39
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:12,981
Two goals ran. Resources, then compiler compile. Build success. Nothing else.

40
00:02:13,531 --> 00:02:16,560
What did that leave behind? Type: ls target

41
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:20,317
The compiled classes. No jar yet, and no test results.

42
00:02:20,867 --> 00:02:21,580
Now the test phase.

43
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:24,771
Type: mvn -B test | grep -E '^\[INFO\] --- |Tests run:.*Skipped: 0$|BUILD' | cut -c8-

44
00:02:28,101 --> 00:02:32,794
Sure fire starts a fresh Java process for the tests. That takes a few seconds.

45
00:02:42,344 --> 00:02:43,640
Look at the order.

46
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:44,359
Resources,

47
00:02:44,359 --> 00:02:44,935
compile,

48
00:02:44,935 --> 00:02:46,015
test resources,

49
00:02:46,015 --> 00:02:46,950
test compile,

50
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:48,030
then sure fire.

51
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:49,325
Compile ran again,

52
00:02:49,325 --> 00:02:51,340
because test comes after it.

53
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:52,275
One test ran,

54
00:02:52,275 --> 00:02:53,139
no failures.

55
00:02:53,689 --> 00:02:56,185
Now package. Type: mvn -B package | grep -E '^\[INFO\] --- |BUILD' | cut -c8-

56
00:02:59,215 --> 00:03:01,391
Same chain again, one step longer.

57
00:03:10,941 --> 00:03:16,616
The same five goals, and then one more. Jar, jar. Package is the last stop of that chain.

58
00:03:17,166 --> 00:03:20,131
Look inside target. Type: ls target

59
00:03:20,261 --> 00:03:20,746
The jar,

60
00:03:20,746 --> 00:03:21,776
the test classes,

61
00:03:21,776 --> 00:03:23,776
and the sure fire reports folder.

62
00:03:23,776 --> 00:03:25,594
Everything the chain produced.

63
00:03:26,144 --> 00:03:34,528
You can skip the tests. Type: mvn -B package -DskipTests | grep -E 'skipped|BUILD'

64
00:03:39,658 --> 00:03:44,736
Tests are skipped, and the build still succeeds. Useful in a hurry, but never as a habit.

65
00:03:45,286 --> 00:03:50,768
Now the other life cycle. Type: mvn -B clean | grep -E '^\[INFO\] --- |BUILD' | cut -c8-

66
00:03:50,898 --> 00:03:52,456
One goal: clean, clean.

67
00:03:53,006 --> 00:03:55,587
Check the folder. Type: ls target

68
00:03:55,717 --> 00:04:00,240
Gone. Clean deleted the whole target folder, so the next build starts fresh.

69
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:04,947
Go to the demo project. Type: CD, demo.

70
00:04:05,497 --> 00:04:12,985
Now break it on purpose. Type: sed -i 's/Hello, /Hi, /' src/main/java/cloudcart/Hello.java

71
00:04:13,115 --> 00:04:16,315
The code now says Hi, but the test still expects Hello.

72
00:04:16,865 --> 00:04:17,699
Build the package.

73
00:04:17,699 --> 00:04:21,772
Type: mvn -B package | grep -E '^\[INFO\] --- |Tests run:.*Skipped: 0$|BUILD' | cut -c8-

74
00:04:24,302 --> 00:04:25,966
Wait for sure fire to finish.

75
00:04:35,516 --> 00:04:40,593
The test failed, and Maven stopped. There is no jar goal in the list. Build failure.

76
00:04:41,143 --> 00:04:45,602
So is there a jar? Type: ls target/*.jar

77
00:04:45,732 --> 00:04:50,895
No such file. A failed phase stops every phase after it. That is the safety net.

78
00:04:51,445 --> 00:04:56,138
Fix the greeting. Type: sed -i 's/Hi, /Hello, /' src/main/java/cloudcart/Hello.java

79
00:04:57,068 --> 00:04:58,744
Now the full chain.

80
00:04:58,744 --> 00:05:05,623
Type: mvn -B clean verify | grep -E 'Tests run:.*Skipped: 0$|BUILD' | cut -c8-

81
00:05:05,753 --> 00:05:11,470
Two life cycles in one command. Clean first, then the whole default chain, up to verify.

82
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:21,672
One test,

83
00:05:21,672 --> 00:05:22,541
no failures,

84
00:05:22,541 --> 00:05:23,556
build success.

85
00:05:23,556 --> 00:05:27,975
Verify is the last quality gate before you install or deploy.

86
00:05:29,525 --> 00:05:31,125
Five things to carry with you.

87
00:05:31,675 --> 00:05:31,953
One.

88
00:05:31,953 --> 00:05:33,762
You can chain life cycles.

89
00:05:33,762 --> 00:05:36,823
M V N clean package starts fresh every time.

90
00:05:36,823 --> 00:05:37,797
In a pipeline,

91
00:05:37,797 --> 00:05:39,398
that is the safe habit.

92
00:05:39,948 --> 00:05:40,212
Two.

93
00:05:40,212 --> 00:05:41,205
Dash capital D,

94
00:05:41,205 --> 00:05:41,933
skip tests,

95
00:05:41,933 --> 00:05:43,521
skips running the tests.

96
00:05:43,521 --> 00:05:45,772
Never skip them to hide a failure.

97
00:05:46,322 --> 00:05:51,143
Three. Dash B is batch mode. Plain text, no colours. Use it in a pipeline.

98
00:05:51,693 --> 00:05:54,722
Four. Dash Q is quiet. It prints errors only.

99
00:05:55,272 --> 00:05:55,585
Five.

100
00:05:55,585 --> 00:05:56,896
Read the first error.

101
00:05:56,896 --> 00:05:59,394
Maven prints the failing phase and goal.

102
00:05:59,394 --> 00:06:00,143
Start there,

103
00:06:00,143 --> 00:06:01,267
not at the bottom.

104
00:06:03,317 --> 00:06:04,200
Your lab task.

105
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:07,480
Lab eighty-six gives you a project whose tests fail.

106
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,184
Lab check judges your work.

107
00:06:09,734 --> 00:06:11,893
It lives at git hub dot com,

108
00:06:11,893 --> 00:06:13,435
slash it dash waves,

109
00:06:13,435 --> 00:06:15,209
slash dev ops dash A I,

110
00:06:15,209 --> 00:06:16,057
in academy,

111
00:06:16,057 --> 00:06:16,365
lab,

112
00:06:16,365 --> 00:06:18,139
lab eighty-six dot S H.

113
00:06:18,689 --> 00:06:20,146
One: run M V N test,

114
00:06:20,146 --> 00:06:21,384
read the failure,

115
00:06:21,384 --> 00:06:23,861
and fix the bug in price dot java,

116
00:06:23,861 --> 00:06:25,537
until three tests pass.

117
00:06:26,087 --> 00:06:30,389
Two: save the list of goals from M V N package into goals dot text,

118
00:06:30,389 --> 00:06:32,508
with the grep from the task file.

119
00:06:33,058 --> 00:06:38,157
Three: save the skip tests output into skip dot text. It must say tests are skipped.

120
00:06:38,707 --> 00:06:41,480
Four: the checker builds the jar itself,

121
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,144
with M V N clean verify.

122
00:06:43,144 --> 00:06:45,363
Your fix must make that succeed.

123
00:06:45,913 --> 00:06:49,966
Five: finish with M V N clean, so the target folder is gone.

124
00:06:50,516 --> 00:06:52,890
Install a J D K and Maven first.

125
00:06:52,890 --> 00:06:53,780
Then lab up,

126
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:54,522
lab check,

127
00:06:54,522 --> 00:06:55,486
and lab down.

128
00:06:55,486 --> 00:06:58,602
The shortcut file is shortcuts eighty-six.

129
00:07:00,652 --> 00:07:02,721
Pass or fail. You need all six.

130
00:07:03,271 --> 00:07:05,085
Five pass lines in lab check.

131
00:07:05,635 --> 00:07:07,768
You can list the default phases in order.

132
00:07:08,318 --> 00:07:11,049
You can explain why package also runs the tests.

133
00:07:11,599 --> 00:07:14,756
You can name the goal bound to compile, test and package.

134
00:07:15,306 --> 00:07:16,906
You can say what clean deletes.

135
00:07:17,456 --> 00:07:19,376
lab down, nothing left behind.

136
00:07:19,926 --> 00:07:21,227
To pass, all six.

137
00:07:23,277 --> 00:07:26,114
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

138
00:07:26,664 --> 00:07:28,755
One: lab up, and read the task file.

139
00:07:29,305 --> 00:07:32,505
Two: run M V N test, and read the first failure.

140
00:07:33,055 --> 00:07:35,551
Three: fix the bug until three tests pass.

141
00:07:36,101 --> 00:07:39,045
Four: save goals dot text and skip dot text.

142
00:07:39,595 --> 00:07:42,646
Five: finish with M V N clean, and lab check.

143
00:07:43,196 --> 00:07:45,777
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

144
00:07:46,327 --> 00:07:48,162
Pause the video, and begin now.

145
00:08:03,712 --> 00:08:04,587
Quick check.

146
00:08:05,137 --> 00:08:07,121
Name the default phases, in order.

147
00:08:07,671 --> 00:08:09,761
Why does package also run the tests?

148
00:08:10,311 --> 00:08:12,445
Which goal is bound to the package phase?

149
00:08:12,995 --> 00:08:14,232
What does clean delete?

150
00:08:14,782 --> 00:08:17,961
Objective covered: M C ten, objective two.

151
00:08:18,511 --> 00:08:20,580
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

152
00:08:31,130 --> 00:08:35,034
Next: plug ins, properties, profiles and reproducible builds.

153
00:08:35,584 --> 00:08:38,912
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
